    {
      "id": "a4e29c3a-a46e-4fb1-88ee-86bbc3885ebc",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Workflow Documentation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -160,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 588,
        "content": "# DeFi Liquidation Risk Monitor\n\nThis workflow runs every ten minutes to monitor a DeFi lending position for liquidation risk. It loads API endpoints and health factor thresholds, fetches the live lending position and collateral market price, then validates both responses. It calculates health factor, liquidation price, and distance to liquidation, and classifies risk using warning 1.5, critical 1.2, and urgent 1.1 thresholds. Every cycle is logged to Google Sheets. Alerts fire only on risk state change or escalation, are summarized by AI, sent to Slack, and stored in alert history.\n\n## Setup Steps:\n\n1. Set the schedule interval for the monitoring cycle, defaulting to every ten minutes.\n2. Configure the production lending position API endpoint and the production market price API endpoint in the monitor configuration node, including warning 1.5, critical 1.2, and urgent 1.1 thresholds.\n3. Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the Monitoring History and Alert History sheets used for cycle logging and alert auditing.\n4. Connect OpenAI credentials and select the production model used to generate risk alert summaries.\n5. Connect Slack credentials and select the channel that should receive liquidation risk alerts.\n6. Activate the workflow and confirm the first successful monitoring cycle writes to Monitoring History before relying on production alerts."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
